    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI found out by complete accident that neovim will send a fetch request if you accidentally use 'gf' or try to edit a `http` link. This feature is from `runtime/plugin/net.lua` and can be disabled by setting `g:loaded_nvim_net_plugin` to a non-nil value. I find the fact somewhat disconcerting that neovim, through a undocumented feature, will pretty much go ahead and do a network request without any confirmation or prior knowledge, even if the threat model is somewhat non-existent, although there is at least a notification of such. For one, `vim.pack` asks for confirmation though it is impossible to accidentally use.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n1. Ideally the plugin would be documented and discoverable.\n2. The plugin should be disabled by default or there should at least an opt-out preemptive confirmation prompt.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
