            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> a similar feature has existed in Vim's \"netrw\", for ~20 years\n> \n> what else do you expect when you `:edit` or `gf` on a URL ?\n\nI vaguely know of the capability in netrw but I have never used it or even gotten close to accidentally proccing it. Meanwhile I sometimes mean to press `gx` to view something in a browser and press `gf` from muscle memory which leads to neovim taking a non insignificant amount in time in fetching raw, likely useless html. To be blunt if I `gf` on a url I expect to get a empty buffer. Not that the functionality is bad, but a little documentation would go a long way.",
